ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: red
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [
  "On a small-story single-doc CoQA setup, 'in-context residency' and 'past-query similarity' are near-isomorphic: both indices live in the same low-dimensional topical manifold the dialog walks, so cosine(q, window) and cosine(q, past-queries) trivially co-fire. The zero gate−cache delta is the EXPECTED outcome of base-rate topical autocorrelation, not a surprising empirical finding.",
  "Redundancy fraction M1=0.532 is a direct consequence of CoQA's design (each turn references prior turns over one short story); it is not evidence for a general agent-RAG redundancy law. >20% is over-determined here.",
  "AUC ~0.55 for both lexical and MiniLM is the predicted ceiling when GT is defined by chunk identity on a corpus of ~tens of short sentences: query lexical/semantic overlap with the live window is a weak proxy for 'this specific gold chunk is resident' simply because many resident chunks are topically similar. Near-chance AUC is what basic IR theory predicts, not a surprise.",
  "The L0's AUC 0.84–1.00 collapsing to ~0.55 is the textbook generator-tautology / distribution-shift effect (item-id seeded text), exactly what any skeptic would have predicted pre-hoc. Calling it a 'finding' overstates."
]
CONFOUNDS: [
  "Single-document, single-hop QA confounds 'live-window residency' with 'topical proximity to the only story present' — the cache and gate are measured on the same manifold, so equivalence is structurally guaranteed, not empirically discovered.",
  "W=6 live window + dialogs of comparable length means the 'live window' frequently ≈ 'entire seen history' ≈ 'past-query set', collapsing the conceptual distinction by construction.",
  "Top-1 retrieval==gold rate of 0.434 means ~57% of 'retrievals' are wrong anyway; gate-vs-cache F1 differences are diluted by retrieval noise unrelated to the gating mechanism.",
  "Qwen2.5-1.5B is small enough that downstream F1 differences may be floored/ceilinged by model capability rather than by what was injected — masking any real gate/cache divergence at the input level.",
  "Matched skip-rate is matched in AGGREGATE, not in WHICH turns are skipped; gate and cache may skip largely overlapping turn-sets in this regime, mechanically forcing F1 parity."
]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [
  "That CoQA-as-RAG generalizes to multi-doc, multi-hop, long-horizon agent traces where 'live window' and 'past queries' can diverge (different docs, different sub-tasks). Researcher flags this honestly but the negative is then narrower than the operational-death framing.",
  "That GT_INCONTEXT defined via answer_start offsets within W=6 is the right ground truth — no sensitivity analysis on W (e.g. W=3, W=12) reported.",
  "That A-RAG's Context Tracker is operationally identical to the proposed gate at the algorithmic level — no head-to-head reimplementation, only a textual collision is documented (sufficient for novelty kill, insufficient for 'A-RAG would also tie the cache')."
]
STATISTICAL_GAPS: [
  "n=1,868 paired turns; gate−cache F1 CI [−0.0045,+0.0053] is consistent with both true-zero AND a small positive effect (~0.5 F1 pt) — 'zero measurable difference' is honest, 'operationally meaningless' is a stronger claim the CI alone does not license without a pre-registered TOST equivalence margin (none stated).",
  "Skip-overlap between gate and cache (Jaccard of skipped-turn sets) not reported — without it we cannot tell whether F1 parity is because the two policies skip the SAME turns (trivial) or DIFFERENT turns with coincidentally equal accuracy (non-trivial). This is the single most diagnostic missing statistic.",
  "Only one LLM, one embedding, one dataset, one W; no seed variance on the LLM generations reported (vLLM temperature/sampling config not in packet).",
  "Precision Δ CI at skip=0.10 is +0.057 [+0.022,+0.090] — a real, CI-significant gate>cache edge at low skip, dismissed as 'only at lowest skip' without engagement; at low-skip / high-precision deployments this is the regime that matters most for latency-budget gating."
]
RATIONALE: The L1 is methodologically clean and the honest negative is creditable, but the theoretical framing claiming 'OPERATIONALLY DEAD / N1 fires' overreaches the evidence in two ways. (1) The gate≈cache equivalence on CoQA is the PREDICTED outcome of measuring two topical-proximity indices on a single short story with W≈history-length — it is a structural confound of the setup, not a property of the gating concept on real agent+RAG. The packet itself flags this limitation. (2) The CI is an absence-of-evidence interval, not an equivalence test; no TOST margin was pre-registered, and the missing skip-overlap statistic is the one that would actually distinguish 'same skips, trivially equal' from 'different skips, accidentally equal'. The N4 prior-art kill (A-RAG Context Tracker, arXiv 2602.03442 verbatim 'records which chunks have been READ ... to prevent redundant information retrieval') is real and load-bearing — that alone justifies REFUTED-on-novelty independently. Vote RED because the verdict text claims more than the experiment licenses (operational-death on a setup that structurally guarantees the null) while simultaneously being correct on the narrower novelty-kill — the right map delta is 'refuted on novelty (N4), inconclusive on N1 pending multi-doc/long-horizon trace where gate and cache can diverge'. Cites: A-RAG arXiv 2602.03442 §3; GPTCache (zilliz.com); GPT Semantic Cache arXiv 2411.05276; CoQA Reddy et al. 2018 (single-doc conversational QA design).
